A||||5||86 SE||Emblem fell off||||1||
Z||000000||86 SE||06-06-2000||04:31 PM||||The other day I was at the car wash, I was washing it & the front emblem fell off can u tell me what I need to use to put it back on with<BR>thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||06-06-2000||05:28 PM||||Try a dab of clear silicone (in a pinch, a dab of RTV silicone will work too).<P>As long as you don't use too much, any color will do, because you won't see it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||06-06-2000||11:22 PM||||The best thing to stick it good is polyurethane. It's the stuff they use to hold the windshield in place.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||06-07-2000||12:34 AM||||Did it just fall off, or did it break? Is there one bigger plastic stud and one tiny locator thing still sticking out the back, if so, then you just need to find one of those weird little nut things to screw it back on. If it's broken, you have to glue it back on or get a new or used emblem. Check the salvage yards, the nut is a 10mm size, I believe.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 06-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||06-07-2000||01:03 AM||||Mine fell off, and I used some 3m weatherstrip adhesive to glue it back on.  that stuff rules!||||reg||1
Z||000005||prof bobo||06-08-2000||01:23 AM||||JB Weld.  Unless you _ever_ want to remove it again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
